      <CodeBlock code={"\n\nCURRENT_ISSUER=$(oc get authentication cluster -o jsonpath='{.spec.serviceAccountIssuer}')\nGCP_BUCKET=$(echo ${CURRENT_ISSUER} | cut -d \"/\" -f4)\nCLUSTER_NAME=${GCP_BUCKET%-*}\n\n"} lang="text" />
      <Alert variant="note" class="my-4">
        <AlertTitle>Note</AlertTitle>
        <AlertDescription>
          <p>Your cluster might differ from this example, and the resource names might not be derived identically from the cluster name. Ensure that you specify the correct corresponding resource names for your cluster.</p>
        </AlertDescription>
      </Alert>
      </li>
      <li>
      Create a temporary directory to use and assign it an environment variable by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ TEMPDIR=$(mktemp -d)"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      To cause the Kubernetes API server to create a new bound service account signing key, you delete the next bound service account signing key.
      <Alert variant="info" class="my-4">
        <AlertTitle>Important</AlertTitle>
